 "title": "Zinc Homeostasis in Escherichia coli and Yeast Cells",
 "summary": "This cluster revolves around zinc homeostasis in Escherichia coli and yeast cells. Zinc (Zn) is a crucial element that is bound to Zn coordination complexes and has a concentration in the cytosol. The ZRT1 gene in E. coli regulates Zn import. In yeast cells, Zn is present in the cytosol and modulated by ZnS QDs, which also affect the mitochondrion. The pos5Δ gene is down-regulated in response to ZnS QDs and ZnSO4 exposure. Various methods and tools, such as CYT10 and FTS, are used to study Zn concentration and homeostasis.",
